# Eta Formatter Safety

When modifying formatter logic, preserve Eta semantics and only change formatting.

## Semantics First

- Treat Eta tag behavior as source of truth from <https://eta.js.org/>.
- Keep support expectations clear for `<%=`, `<%~`, and `<% ... %>`.
- Preserve block comments in Eta form (`/* ... */`) without semantic rewrite.
- Respect whitespace control markers (`-`) and avoid destructive normalization.

## Algorithm Boundaries

- Keep indentation decisions explicit and deterministic.
- Avoid mutating JavaScript expressions inside Eta tags unless required.
- For mixed Eta+HTML lines, ensure split/reflow does not reorder content.

## Required Example Coverage

For formatter edits, provide at least these input/output examples:
- Eta-only block with nested braces.
- HTML with nested tags and Eta interpolation.
- Mixed line where `%>` is followed by HTML.

